### Implementation
Repla..."
US-014 is complete. All acceptance criteria are met, with one important bug found along the way.

**What was implemented**

- **Hardcoded role checks replaced with `hasPermission(...)`** across all components that gated capabilities by role: `ProyectoDetalle.jsx` (Nueva Versión / Subir Documento / PDF buttons, back-link, info panels), `DocumentViewer.jsx` ("Marcar como Revisado" → `APPROVE_DOCUMENT`, commenting → `COMMENT_DOCUMENT`), `CommentsPanel.jsx` (`MANAGE_COMMENTS`), `ProjectsTable.jsx` (`UPDATE_PROJECT`/`DELETE_PROJECT`), and `Navbar.jsx` (menus, notification bell, admin link). `Administration.jsx` was already fully permission-driven from US-013, so nothing to replace there. Role checks remain only where they're genuinely about routing (ProtectedRoute, post-login redirect), not capabilities.
- **Critical backend bug fix**: `getMyPermissions` (US-009) populated a nonexistent `rol` relation — the user schema defines `rols` — so the endpoint always returned an empty list and every permission gate added since US-010 was invisible to all users. It now merges active permission codes across all of the user's roles.
- **Seeder now grants permissions to Tutor and Estudiante roles** (previously only Coordinador and Admin got any), refactored into a role→permissions map.
- **Consistent denied messages**: new `AccessDenied` component with a shared `ACCESS_DENIED_MESSAGE`, used as a page-level `VIEW_AUDIT_LOGS` gate in `AuditLogs.jsx`.
- **`hasPermission(code)` added to PermissionContext** so components can write `{hasPermission("APPROVE_DOCUMENT") && <ApproveBtn/>}` exactly as the AC specifies.

**Quality checks**

- 15 new permission tests, all passing (PermissionGate, AccessDenied, ProjectsTable, CommentsPanel, Navbar). One gotcha: CRA's default `resetMocks: true` wipes `jest.mock` factory implementations, so mocks are configured in `beforeEach`.
- `npm run typecheck` passes; `npm run lint` now passes with **0 errors** — down from 84 pre-existing ones, cleared via eslint config fixes (jest globals for tests, jsx-runtime, ignoring vendored k6 scripts) plus mechanical fixes (unused imports, missing PropTypes) in the affected files.

Learnings and reusable patterns were appended to `.ralph-tui/progress.md`.

